    "custom_info_cards_GaPaxf": {
      "type": "custom-info-cards",
      "blocks": {
        "info_card_fYQgCq": {
          "type": "info_card",
          "settings": {
            "variant_ids": "",
            "desktop_image": "shopify://shop_images/01.Neurological_Health.jpg",
            "image_alt": "",
            "heading": "Neurological Health",
            "description": "<p>Multiple peer-reviewed studies have identified associations between prolonged high-fluoride water consumption and cognitive effects — particularly in developing children. Reducing daily fluoride intake through filtered water is a meaningful precautionary step many families are taking today.</p>",
            "enable_accordion_mobile": true,
            "enable_accordion_desktop": false,
            "tag": ""
          }
        },
        "info_card_477mBi": {
          "type": "info_card",
          "settings": {
            "variant_ids": "",
            "desktop_image": "shopify://shop_images/02.Thyroid_Function.jpg",
            "image_alt": "",
            "heading": "Hormonal Balance",
            "description": "<p>The thyroid regulates your metabolism, energy, and hormonal equilibrium. Research suggests prolonged fluoride exposure may interfere with thyroid activity — especially in people with iodine deficiency — making fluoride-reduced water an increasingly important wellness priority.</p>",
            "enable_accordion_mobile": true,
            "enable_accordion_desktop": false,
            "tag": ""
          }
        },
        "info_card_Ukdnxc": {
          "type": "info_card",
          "settings": {
            "variant_ids": "",
            "desktop_image": "shopify://shop_images/03.Skeletal_Health.jpg",
            "image_alt": "",
            "heading": "Bone & Joint Integrity",
            "description": "<p>While fluoride plays a role in dental strength at controlled levels, excess fluoride over time has been linked to skeletal fluorosis — a condition affecting bones and joints with symptoms ranging from stiffness to structural changes. Long-term reduction is your best insurance.</p>",
            "enable_accordion_mobile": true,
            "enable_accordion_desktop": false,
            "tag": ""
          }
        },
        "info_card_W4BWXx": {
          "type": "info_card",
          "settings": {
            "variant_ids": "",
            "desktop_image": "shopify://shop_images/04._Low_Birth_Weight.jpg",
            "image_alt": "",
            "heading": "Pregnancy & Birth Outcomes",
            "description": "<p>Scientific literature has explored a potential association between elevated fluoride exposure during pregnancy and increased risks of low birth weight and preterm delivery. For expectant mothers, reducing fluoride in drinking water is a straightforward and proactive protective measure.</p>",
            "enable_accordion_mobile": true,
            "enable_accordion_desktop": false,
            "tag": ""
          }
        }
      },
